🚀 Start with
To run the gamebook generator from the terminal, use the following command:

python3 gamebook-generator_1.py --prompt "Post-apocalyptic wasteland where humanity is rebuilding after a mysterious global event."
================================================================================================================================================================
The --prompt parameter allows you to set the theme and atmosphere of your game. The AI will generate the starting scene along with branching narrative choices.
================================================================================================================================================================
📝 Editing in Twine
Import to Twine
The generated .twee file can be imported into the Twine editor:

Open Twine.

Click “Import from file”.

Select the .twee file (e.g., generated_game.twee).

Export as HTML
Once your story is ready in Twine:

Click the gear icon.

Choose “Publish to File” – this will export a .html file containing your entire game.


